The UE sets the **SLRB-PC5-ConfigIndex** included in the slrb-ConfigToReleaseList corresponding to the sidelink DRB.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 1 > for each sidelink DRB that is to be released, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1.1, due to configuration by sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or by upper layers: 2 > set the SLRB-PC5-ConfigIndex included in the slrb-ConfigToReleaseList corresponding to the sidelink DRB;

The UE sets the **SLRB-Config** included in the slrb-ConfigToAddModList, according to the received sl-RadioBearerConfig and sl-RLC-BearerConfig corresponding to the sidelink DRB.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 1 > for each sidelink DRB that is to be established or modified, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2.1, due to receiving sl- ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR: 2 > set the SLRB-Config included in the slrb-ConfigToAddModList, according to the received sl- RadioBearerConfig and sl-RLC-BearerConfig corresponding to the sidelink DRB;

Based on TS 38.331, if the UE is in (NG)EN-DC, is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration in an RRCReconfiguration received over SRB3, and the message was received as part of ConditionalReconfiguration, the UE shall:

> continue using the configuration used prior to when the inability to comply with the RRCReconfiguration message was detected;

and

> continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of RRCReconfiguration message;

This behavior is specified for the conditional reconfiguration case, where the UE does not initiate failure recovery (like SCG failure information or re-establishment) but instead reverts to the previous configuration.

In (NG)EN-DC, if the UE is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration in an RRCReconfiguration received over SRB3 and MCG transmission is not suspended, the UE initiates the **SCG failure information procedure** to report an SCG reconfiguration error.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> if the UE is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration included in the RRCReconfiguration message received over SRB3; ... if MCG transmission is not suspended: initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration error, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends;

The procedure in clause 5.7.9.1 specifies how to store **handover failure information in VarRLF-Report**.

**Supporting quote from the context:**
> 3 > store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in the clause 5.3.10.5;

The UE shall perform Reconfiguration with sync according to 5.3.5.5.2.

**Supporting quote from context:**
> 1 > if the CellGroupConfig contains the spCellConfig with reconfigurationWithSync: 2 > perform Reconfiguration with sync according to 5.3.5.5.2;

The UE shall immediately acquire the requested SI message(s) as defined in clause 5.2.2.3.2.

**Supporting context excerpt:**
> if acknowledgement for SI request is received from lower layers: 3 > acquire the requested SI message(s) as defined in clause 5.2.2.3.2, immediately;

Based on TS 38.331, when the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12, and sl-SyncPriority for the concerned frequency is not configured or is set to gnss, and GNSS is reliable, the UE shall select GNSS as the synchronization reference source.

**Quoted context:**
> 1 > else if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl- ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12, and sl-SyncPriority for the concerned frequency is not configured or is set to gnss, and GNSS is reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 and TS 38.133 : 2 > select GNSS as the synchronization reference source;

The UE sets `measResultIdleEUTRA` in the UEInformationResponse **if the idleModeMeasurementReq is included in the UEInformationRequest and the UE has stored VarMeasIdleReport that contains measurement information concerning cells other than the PCell, and if measReportIdleEUTRA is available in the VarMeasIdleReport**.

**Supporting context excerpt:**
> if the idleModeMeasurementReq is included in the UEInformationRequest and the UE has stored VarMeasIdleReport that contains measurement information concerning cells other than the PCell: 2 > set the measResultIdleEUTRA in the UEInformationResponse message to the value of measReportIdleEUTRA in the VarMeasIdleReport, if available;

For condEventA3, A4, or A5, the UE considers the event associated to a measId to be not fulfilled when the leaving condition(s) applicable for that event are fulfilled for the applicable cells for all measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during the corresponding timeToTrigger defined for the event within the VarConditionalReconfig.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 3 > if the condEventId is associated with condEventA3, condEventA4 or condEventA5, and if the leaving condition(s) applicable for this event associated with the condReconfigId, i.e. the event corresponding with the condEventId(s) of the corresponding condTriggerConfig within VarConditionalReconfig, is fulfilled for the applicable cells for all measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during the corresponding timeToTrigger defined for this event within the VarConditionalReconfig: 4 > consider the event associated to that measId to be not fulfilled;

When events for all measIds within condTriggerConfig for a target candidate cell are fulfilled, the UE considers that target candidate cell as a triggered cell and initiates the conditional reconfiguration execution.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 2 > if event(s) associated to all measId(s) within condTriggerConfig for a target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig are fulfilled:  
> 3 > consider the target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig, associated to that condReconfigId, as a triggered cell;  
> 3 > initiate the conditional reconfiguration execution, as specified in 5.3.5.13.5;

The UE sets the `measurementIndication` to `nr-PRS-Measurement` when the procedure is initiated for positioning measurement towards NR.

**Supporting context excerpt:**
> 2 > else if the procedure is initiated for positioning measurement towards NR: 3 > set the measurementIndication to the nr-PRS-Measurement according to the information received from upper layers;

The UE shall forward the ue-Identity, accessType (if present) and paging cause (if determined) to the upper layers.

**Supporting extract from context:**
> if upper layers indicate the support of paging cause: 4 > forward the ue-Identity, accessType (if present) and paging cause (if determined) to the upper layers;

If the L2 U2N Relay UE receives a Paging message and a PagingRecord's ue-Identity matches a sl-PagingIdentity-RemoteUE, it shall initiate the Uu Message transfer in sidelink as specified in 5.8.9.9.

**Supporting context:**
> if the ue-Identity included in the PagingRecord in the Paging message matches the UE identity in sl- PagingIdentity-RemoteUE included in sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE: inititate the Uu Message transfer in sidelink as specified in 5.8.9.9;

For an NR cell with reportType set to eventTriggered, the UE considers the quantity used in the aN-Offset as the sorting quantity for eventA3.

**Exact quote from context:**  
> for an NR cell, consider the quantity used in the aN-Offset (for eventA3 and eventA6) as the sorting quantity;

> if the current configuration contains a Uu Relay RLC channel with the received uu-Relay-RLC-ChannelID within the same cell group:  
> 2> if reestablishRLC is received:  
> 3> re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322 ;  
> 2> reconfigure the RLC entity in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
> 2> reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig;

**Answer:** It shall re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322, reconfigure the RLC entity in accordance with the received rlc-Config, and reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.

If the RRCReestablishment message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig, the UE shall perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16 and consider the current cell to be the PCell.

**Quoted from context:**
> 1 > if the RRCReestablishment message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig (i.e. the UE is a L2 U2N Remote UE): 2 > perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16; 2 > consider the current cell to be the PCell;

When entering RRC_CONNECTED, if an L2 U2N Remote UE had previously sent sl-Requested-SI-List and sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE, it shall:

> set the sl-Requested-SI-List to the value release;
> set the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE to the value release;
> submit the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.

*(This answer is directly extracted from the provided context.)*

Access categories 0 and 2 are exempt from access barring when RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers.

**Supporting context excerpt:**
> 1 > if RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: 2 > inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';

For a L2 U2N Relay UE in RRC_IDLE, an RRC connection establishment is initiated in the following case:

> if any message is received from a L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 as specified in 9.1.1.4 or SL-RLC1 as specified in 9.2.4;

This is an exact statement from the provided context.

After stopping the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322 for a measId during quantity configuration, the UE shall **reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId**.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 2 > stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever one is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId;

If the RRCResume message does not include the `restoreMCG-SCells`, the UE shall release the MCG SCell(s) from the stored UE Inactive AS context.

**Exact quote from the context:**
> 2 > if the RRCResume does not include the restoreMCG-SCells: 3 > release the MCG SCell(s) from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;

After handling the associated sl-MeasIds (i.e., removing their reporting entries and stopping/resetting their timers), the UE **reconfigures the existing sl-MeasObjectId entry with the value received for this sl-MeasObject**.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 3 &gt; reconfigure the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasObject;

If the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging, the UE shall:

1. Select '0' as the Access Category.
2. Perform the unified access control procedure using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers.
3. If the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends.

*Quote from context:*
> 1 > if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging:  
> 2 > select '0' as the Access Category;  
> 2 > perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers;  
> 3 > if the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends;

When the conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with clause 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled, the UE:

1. Considers the resume procedure is initiated for SDT.
2. Starts timer T319a.
3. Starts timer T319.
4. Instructs the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running.

This is explicitly stated in the provided context:

> 1 > if conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled:
> 2 > consider the resume procedure is initiated for SDT;
> 2 > start timer T319a;
> 2 > start timer T319;
> 2 > instruct the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running;

Based on TS 38.331, when the UE initiates transmission of the SCGFailureInformation message due to an indication from SCG RLC that the maximum number of retransmissions has been reached, the UE sets the **failureType** to **rlc-MaxNumRetx**.

The provided context confirms this exact statement:
> else if the UE initiates transmission of the SCGFailureInformation message to provide indication from SCG RLC that the maximum number of retransmissions has been reached: 2 > set the failureType as rlc-MaxNumRetx;

The UE shall perform the sidelink quantity configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.8.

**Supporting Context Excerpt:**
> 1 > if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-QuantityConfig in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink: 2 > perform the sidelink quantity configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.8;

After assembling and forwarding the complete warning message, the UE shall **stop assembling a warning message and geographical area coordinates (if any) for this messageIdentifier and serialNumber and delete all stored information held for it**. This includes discarding the stored warningMessageSegment(s) used in the assembly.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 4 &gt; stop assembling a warning message and geographical area coordinates (if any) for this messageIdentifier and serialNumber and delete all stored information held for it;

When T304 of a secondary cell group expires and MCG transmission is not suspended, the UE initiates the SCG failure information procedure to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure.

**Supporting context excerpt:**  
> 1 > else if T304 of a secondary cell group expires:  
> 2 > if MCG transmission is not suspended:  
> 3 > release dedicated preambles provided in rach-ConfigDedicated, if configured;  
> 3 > **initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure**, upon which the RRC reconfiguration procedure ends;

When the SCG failure information procedure is initiated (and it is **not** due to beam failure of the PSCell while the SCG is deactivated), the UE shall suspend SCG transmission for **all SRBs, all DRBs, and, if any, BH RLC channels**.

**Supporting extract from the context:**  
> 2 > suspend SCG transmission for all SRBs, DRBs and, if any, BH RLC channels;

The UE applies a timing advance of **mgta ms** before the calculated gap subframe occurrences.

**Supporting extract from context:**
> apply the specified timing advance mgta to the gap occurrences calculated above (i.e. the UE starts the measurement mgta ms before the gap subframe occurrences);

Upon successful handover completion, the UE shall release the AS security context including the K<sub>RRCenc</sub> key, the K<sub>RRCint</sub> key, the K<sub>UPint</sub> key and the K<sub>UPenc</sub> key, if stored.

*Quote from context:*
> release the AS security context including the K key, the K key, the K key and the K key, if stored;

For the measId that triggered the reporting, the UE shall first set the measId to the measurement identity that triggered the measurement reporting within the MeasurementReport message.

**Quote from context:**
> For the measId for which the measurement reporting procedure was triggered, the UE shall set the measResults within the MeasurementReport message as follows: 1 > set the measId to the measurement identity that triggered the measurement reporting;

Based on TS 38.331, if a UE in RRC_CONNECTED receives an RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink, it shall perform the **sidelink UE information procedure for NR sidelink communication**.

The provided context contains the exact statement confirming this requirement:
> if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED: 2 > perform the sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication procedure, as specified in 5.8.3.3 or clause 5.10.15 in TS 36.331 ;

The value of the **sl-PhysCellId** is used as the physical cell identity of the PCell.

**Quoted context:**  
> 2 > use the value of the sl-PhysCellId as the physical cell identity of the PCell;

If the RRCReconfiguration includes the **scg-State**, the UE shall:

> perform SCG deactivation as specified in 5.3.5.13b;  
> perform SCG activation as specified in 5.3.5.13a;

This is explicitly stated in the provided context (the first few lines of the first excerpt). The order indicates the UE first deactivates the SCG (if currently active) and then activates it (if the scg-State indicates activation).

For each DAPS bearer, when the RRCReconfiguration includes **daps‑SourceRelease**, the UE shall:

> release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
> reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323.

Based on TS 38.331, if the procedure was initiated due to reception of the sk-Counter and the UE is in NE-DC, or NR-DC, or is configured with SN terminated bearer(s), the UE shall:

1. Derive or update the secondary key (S-KgNB or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501.
2. Derive the KRRCenc key and the KUPenc key as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-KgNB or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse.
3. Derive the KRRCint key and the KUPint key as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-KgNB or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse.

*Quote from context:*
> 1> else if this procedure was initiated due to reception of the sk-Counter (UE is in NE-DC, or NR-DC, or is configured with SN terminated bearer(s)):
> 2> derive or update the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501 ;
> 2> derive the K key and the K key as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse;
> 2> derive the K key and the K key as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse;

Based on TS 38.331, for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission, the UE sets `sl-QoS-InfoList` to include the QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) of the associated destination configured by the upper layer.

**Supporting Context Excerpt:**
> 5> set sl-QoS-InfoList to include QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) of the associated destination configured by the upper layer for the NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;

Based on TS 38.331, when a UE is acting as an NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay UE and includes this information in the `SidelinkUEInformationNR` message, it sets the `ue-Type` field to **relayUE**.

**Supporting Context Excerpt:**
> 4 > include ue-Type and set it to relayUE if the UE is acting as NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay UE and to remoteUE otherwise;

Based on TS 38.331, for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission, the UE sets **sl-TxInterestedFreqList** to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission.

**Supporting context excerpt:**
> 5> set sl-TxInterestedFreqList to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;

Upon detecting sidelink radio link failure for a specific destination, the UE discards the NR sidelink communication related configuration of that destination.

**Supporting context extract:**  
> 2 > discard the NR sidelink communication related configuration of this destination;
